## Biggest Realization

- SQL is just a language. The real skill is understanding how the database thinks.
- Before writing SQL, I should understand the business requirements first.
- Database design starts with planning the entities and relationships, not by immediately creating tables.
- I should start asking "Why?" instead of memorizing syntax.
